The federal government was prepared to send $175 million of your money to people who were already dead, a staggering example of how badly Washington can lose track of taxpayer dollars.

@USTreasury caught those payments by screening $3.7 trillion before the money went out, and the same fraud prevention system is now available across 99% of federal programs, up from just 4% last year.

Americans should not have to accept billions lost to fraud as the cost of doing business in Washington.
